; Hand-made roof for Promptholm Town Hall.
;
; This scene carries its own geometry, so PrefabOverrides hands it the whole Roof slot of the one
; building whose roof piece id is "roof_townhall_cupola" — the town hall — and the procedural hip
; roof is never built for it. Every other prefab in this tree is hollow (an empty Node3D plus a
; [Tool] script that builds at runtime) and is therefore ignored.
;
; Authored in slot space: y = 0 is the top of the walls, the plan is centred on the origin, and
; -Z is the front of the building. Sized for the town hall's 5.04 m footprint plus its 0.26 m
; eaves, i.e. 5.56 m across. Change the wall height or the footprint on the server and this roof
; does not follow — that is the trade a hand-made prefab makes, and the reason to author one only
; where the building earns it.
;
; Two crossing gables rather than a pyramid, for a reason worth keeping: a cone or a four-sided
; cap has to be a CylinderMesh with radial_segments = 4, whose vertices sit on the axes, so it
; needs a 45-degree yaw to put its corners over the building's corners — and a rotated mesh has
; a conservative AABB, which VerifyMetricsRunner reads as a footprint twice the real one. Boxes
; and prisms on the axes measure exactly what they are.

